From 932aad5853b9e7193b0007e296a2224b8fe9f06b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 11:35:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] soc/interconnect/axi: AXIDownConverter handles FIXED
 bursts properly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous AXIDownConverter silently translated BURST_FIXED to
BURST_INCR on the narrow side. That worked for FIXED-1 (a single
wide beat is equivalent to a single-beat INCR after splitting),
but corrupted FIXED bursts of length > 1: the narrow side
marched forward (length*ratio narrow beats stepping by
narrow_size each) instead of repeating the same wide-beat-sized
window per wide beat.

AXI4 has no native "INCR within a wide-beat window then reset"
burst type, so the converter cannot express the right semantics
in a single narrow burst. Add a slow-path FSM that issues
`len + 1` independent narrow INCR-`ratio` bursts back-to-back,
all at the captured wide address, alternating between AW emission
and B reception:

  IDLE -> [FIXED-EMIT-AW -> FIXED-WAIT-B]^(len+1) -> FIXED-EMIT-B

The W stream's `last` is overridden when a FIXED burst is in
flight so each ratio-block of narrow beats terminates as its own
narrow burst (the slave needs `last` to commit each B). The R
path mirrors this: AR FSM issues N narrow ARs, each followed by
draining its `ratio` narrow R beats (merged by the StrideConverter
into one wide R beat), and r.last is overridden to fire only on
the final wide beat. The L narrow B responses are coalesced
into one wide B with the worst response winning (RESP_OKAY < ...
< RESP_DECERR).

INCR / WRAP / FIXED-1 keep the original combinational fast path
unchanged, so the common case has no added latency.

Test coverage:

  - The pre-existing test_axi_down_converter_fixed_burst was
    pinning the broken behavior; flipped to verify correctness.
  - Sub-tests now cover: FIXED-1 round-trip; FIXED-2 write
    (only beat[1] survives at X, X+8 untouched); FIXED-4 read
    (every wide beat returns the value at X); FIXED-8 write
    (only beat[7] survives at X).
  - All previous tests stay green: test_axi_down_converter_burst,
    _wrap, _back_to_back, _id_and_last (the INCR/WRAP/back-to-back
    fast paths are unchanged).

Verified: 74 + 29 subtests passing across test_axi.py /
test_axi_lite.py / test_wishbone.py. digilent_arty builds clean
on both --bus-standard=wishbone (778 KB) and --bus-standard=axi
(1017 KB) — no SoC-side regression.

